WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.467
Lesson six.

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.113
Evolution in flight.

00:00:03.113 --> 00:00:06.763
What does the best pilot look like along the way?

00:00:07.363 --> 00:00:13.002
Here is the best pilot from different points in training, all facing the same start.

00:00:13.002 --> 00:00:20.228
A random pilot, then the champions of generations ten, thirty, sixty and one hundred, and the final best.

00:00:20.828 --> 00:00:25.580
The random pilot fires its main engine without a break, and flies away.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.151
The champion of generation ten fires its engines, but still crashes.

00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:33.218
By generation thirty, the best pilot lands.

00:00:33.218 --> 00:00:38.029
Later champions land too, with steadier and more efficient flights.

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:43.401
Here is the centre of the population, drawn as the weight matrix itself.

00:00:43.401 --> 00:00:50.200
The colours are scaled to the biggest weight in each generation, so we can see the pattern while it forms.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.826
At generation zero it is noise.

00:00:53.426 --> 00:00:56.920
The strongest rules in the end are all about speed.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.585
Drifting right fires the left engine.

00:00:59.585 --> 00:01:04.263
Falling fires the main engine, and stops the lander from doing nothing.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:07.702
Spinning clockwise fires the left engine too.
